{"name":"Bro Culture","title":"Bro Culture","revision":229304,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Bro_Culture","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Bro Culture is a broad subculture that stereotypically depicts hypermasculine behaviors and mannerisms commonly found in young men in sports clubs, fraternities, Rock and Metal subcultures, and more recently raves and electronic music festivals."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Philosophy"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"A North American subculture centered on hypermasculinity, the subculture prioritizes group loyalty, physical and/or material achievement, physical toughness, and occassional stoicism, often prioritizing toughness and aggression over vulnerability. However, many bros voice that there is a genuine sense of community and brotherhood in these spaces, and that it provides them a space to be unapologetically and almost radically in touch with their favored variety of masculinity."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"NPR identified four types of bros: dudely, jockish, preppy, and stoner-ish. In their description, dudely bros form close homosocial friendships in a group, jockish bros are defined by ability at team sports tempered by interest in alcohol, preppy bros wear \"conservatively casual\" clothes such as Abercrombie and Fitch and flaunt \"social privilege\", and stoner-ish bros may or may not use cannabis but speak in a relaxed fashion and exude the air of surfers."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Loud / fast cars"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nascar"},{"kind":"list","text":"Motorcycles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Guns"},{"kind":"list","text":"Empty beer cans piling up in garbage cans"},{"kind":"list","text":"Beer cans, energy drink cans, and beer signs as decor"},{"kind":"list","text":"Posters and various decor of sensual / scantily clad women, UFC ring girls"},{"kind":"list","text":"Beer pong tables"},{"kind":"list","text":"MMA octagons, UFC"},{"kind":"list","text":"Trophy cases"},{"kind":"list","text":"Doorway pullup bars"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crosses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vulgar graffiti"},{"kind":"list","text":"Neon signs"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dart boards"},{"kind":"list","text":"Weed paraphernalia"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Saturdays are for the Boys\" flags"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mounted deer heads"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rowing teams"},{"kind":"list","text":"Calvin peeing stickers"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"list","text":"Keg stands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Heavy drinking"},{"kind":"list","text":"Heavy weed smoking"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lacrosse"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tailgating"},{"kind":"list","text":"Raves and Music festivals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cornhole"},{"kind":"list","text":"Playing 2k, FIFA, Halo, or Call of Duty"},{"kind":"list","text":"Arena Rock and Metal concerts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Country music concerts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Snowboarding and Skiing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Flag football"},{"kind":"list","text":"Superbowl parties"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ultimate frisbee"},{"kind":"list","text":"Frisbee golf"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fantasy football leagues"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Bro Culture fashion features cargo shorts, cargo pants, jean shorts (or \"jorts\"), sportswear, camouflage patterns, baseball caps, and t-shirts or hoodies emblazoned with various energy drink logos. A fair comparison could be a more aggressive version of male Normcore fashion."},{"kind":"list","text":"Frayed-brim baseball hats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Oxford shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sports team shirts and jerseys"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cargo shorts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Basketball shorts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Muscle Tees"},{"kind":"list","text":"Boat shoes or sandals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Snapbacks, trucker hats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wrist sweatbands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mullets, pompadours, fades"},{"kind":"list","text":"Goatees, Soul patches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Supreme"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vans, Timberlands, Nikes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ed Hardy, Affliction, Von Dutch, Fox racing, Extreme Couture, Tapout, American Fight"},{"kind":"list","text":"Underarmor"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ralph Lauren"},{"kind":"list","text":"Abercrombie and Fitch"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hollister"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shirts with misogynistic slogans (IE \"Cool Story Babe, Now Make Me a Sandwich\", \"FBI = Female Body Inspector\")."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Unlike many aesthetics, Bro Culture's color palette is not restricted; it can extend throughout the entire color spectrum."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Artists"},{"kind":"list","text":"O.A.R."},{"kind":"list","text":"Dispatch"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dave Matthews Band"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rage Against The Machine"},{"kind":"list","text":"Juice WRLD"},{"kind":"list","text":"Post Malone"},{"kind":"list","text":"Trapt"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kid Rock"},{"kind":"list","text":"Eminem"},{"kind":"list","text":"Avenged Sevenfold"},{"kind":"list","text":"Florida Georgia Line"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pantera"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nickelback"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shinedown"},{"kind":"list","text":"Limp Bizkit"},{"kind":"list","text":"Theory of a Deadman"},{"kind":"list","text":"Five Finger Death Punch"},{"kind":"list","text":"Staind"},{"kind":"list","text":"Linkin Park"},{"kind":"list","text":"Luke Bryan"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hinder"},{"kind":"list","text":"Creed"},{"kind":"list","text":"Buckcherry"},{"kind":"list","text":"Papa Roach"},{"kind":"list","text":"Breaking Benjamin"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hollywood Undead"},{"kind":"list","text":"Seether"},{"kind":"list","text":"12 Stones"},{"kind":"list","text":"Saliva"},{"kind":"list","text":"Drowning Pool"},{"kind":"list","text":"Puddle of Mudd"},{"kind":"list","text":"Three Days Grace"},{"kind":"list","text":"Skillet"},{"kind":"list","text":"Skrillex"},{"kind":"list","text":"Deadmau5"},{"kind":"list","text":"Knife Party"},{"kind":"list","text":"Drake"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nero"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Chainsmokers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Metallica"},{"kind":"list","text":"Slayer"},{"kind":"list","text":"Guns and Roses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Aerosmith"},{"kind":"list","text":"AC/DC"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/25/Bro-classic.jpeg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20210121144404","caption":"Bro-classic","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Bro-classic.jpeg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0137-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/d5/Bro-indie.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20210121144414","caption":"Bro Culture · Visual reference 02","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Bro-indie.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0137-2.webp","localAvailable":true}]}